% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `temporary_standard_io_window`,
% compiled by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS:
% the class is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.6 text
% I/O; §2.14: 2 held programs, create/3).  MENDELS (IFS No.61),
% 2026-11-27: the slot help_tsl_operator of its mendel_editor (and
% med_editor), made when the editor is (editor_com.esp:13-26,
% med_editor.esp:13-26): a "TSL operators" help text that pf11 shows
% (editor_com.esp:88-90).
%
% THE NATURE LIST IS INFERENCE (window.md §1.6: temporary_ names the base
% class, TM-125 p6-7 a temporary window; standard_io_window the text
% I/O): this stand-in is standard_io_window.esp's window, whose methods
% it inherits (erase_cursor/1 among them, added for MENDELS); it has no
% method of its own.  The temporary behaviour (at the mouse, gone when the mouse
% leaves, TM-125 p6-7) is not stood in.

class temporary_standard_io_window has

nature
        standard_io_window;

end.
